ex:TK8_BuildDeck_Ch20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck 2.0.0 (03-materials/ch20/SEN0414_Ch20_EmailTextsPushNotifications_3e_v2_0_0.pptx, 42 slides, 58 code frames, 19 examples) and manifest chapter_code_ch20_v1_0_0.json (Python 3.13.18) built by 08-tooling/chapter_deck_build_v2_3_0.py (adds RESOURCES_ROWS) from 08-tooling/ch20-deck/spec. Checks with logs in 08-tooling/ch20-deck/logs_v2_0_0: material check 8 of 8 clean; manifest self-check pass; overlap check clean; story prose check pass (6 stories); story repeat check ch19-ch20 clean. All 42 rendered slides were looked at: no overlap or cut-off; on slides 17 to 19 the result table sits close to the footer line. Deviations from the approved draft: 42 slides (a fifth analogy slide); ntfy examples build the request with prepare() instead of a local recorder; Gmail examples use a MagicMock stand-in and SMTP examples a local aiosmtpd server, marked EMULATED on the slides; story pictures are a Xerox Alto for the IMAP story (no Lisp machine picture found, said in its credit) and a picture drawn for this deck for the AT&T story (stated on the slide); the resources slide has two columns of eight. Some code slides use 9 pt code. NOT VERIFIED: reviewed conditions (academician, faculty reviewer, undergraduate reader) are not recorded; the page-runs-slide-code and taught-only checks are not built; the verification is by the same agent that built it, so it is not independent." .
ex:ST8_BuildCh20 backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck and manifest done; page with the chapter-code tab remains." .
